---
layout: null
sitemap: false
---
{%- comment -%}
  Search index, fetched lazily on first use by assets/js/search.js.

  Full post bodies are included on purpose: people arrive looking for terms like
  "keepalived VIP" or "depthwise separable convolution", which appear only in
  post text. The whole corpus is ~18k words, so this is roughly 40 KB gzipped —
  cheap enough to ship wholesale, and it costs nothing until someone searches.

  The `hidden` filter must match index.html, or unlisted posts become findable.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign posts = site.posts | where_exp: "p", "p.hidden != true" -%}
[
{%- for post in posts -%}
{
"t": {{ post.title | jsonify }},
"u": {{ post.url | relative_url | jsonify }},
"d": {{ post.date | date: "%b %Y" | jsonify }},
"c": {{ post.categories | jsonify }},
"l": {{ post.lang | default: site.lang | default: 'en' | jsonify }},
"e": {{ post.excerpt | strip_html | strip_newlines | truncate: 200 | jsonify }},
"b": {{ post.content | strip_html | strip_newlines | jsonify }}
}{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
{%- endfor -%}
]
